00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:18.122
I'm in spa...


00:03:18.155 --> 00:03:20.360
David, what's happening??


00:03:25.069 --> 00:03:25.870
Buddy?


00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.107
Buddy, come in!


00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:30.713
Can you hear me,


00:03:30.747 --> 00:03:31.582
David?


00:03:34.021 --> 00:03:35.089
David, David!


00:04:44.761 --> 00:04:45.596
Ew, ew!


00:04:52.343 --> 00:04:53.179
David?


00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.856
Where am I?


00:05:05.837 --> 00:05:06.805
What happened?


00:05:08.843 --> 00:05:10.813
Oh look, a human!


00:05:10.847 --> 00:05:11.682
They'll help!


00:05:13.786 --> 00:05:16.091
Er, excuse me, sir!


00:05:20.933 --> 00:05:22.237
Ahh, a dog, help!


00:05:27.481 --> 00:05:28.716
Oh my gosh, a dog!


00:05:29.951 --> 00:05:31.121
Don't panic!


00:05:31.155 --> 00:05:32.023
I'm dialing 911!


00:05:36.198 --> 00:05:38.202
Stay away from my baby!


00:05:42.844 --> 00:05:44.247
Darned kids!


00:05:44.281 --> 00:05:45.183
Oh jeepers!


00:05:45.216 --> 00:05:46.451
How did I get here?


00:05:47.387 --> 00:05:48.789
Why is everyone so mean?


00:05:49.824 --> 00:05:50.994
David, David!


00:05:51.028 --> 00:05:51.862
Please come in David!


00:05:55.836 --> 00:05:57.907
I don't know what
that is in dog years


00:05:57.941 --> 00:05:59.477
but it's a lot!


00:05:59.512 --> 00:06:00.913
Oh boy,!


00:06:04.854 --> 00:06:05.890
The hatch!


00:06:05.923 --> 00:06:07.827
The space capsule's hatch!


00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.831
It must have broken
off in the re-entry.


00:06:09.864 --> 00:06:13.906
I fell out and so where's
the rest of the capsule gone?


00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:14.808
Where is David?


00:06:17.581 --> 00:06:18.816
And how'd this get here??


00:06:22.223 --> 00:06:23.859
Of course!


00:06:23.892 --> 00:06:26.265
A friendly neighborhood
police officer will help me!


00:06:28.969 --> 00:06:31.775
Oh, but he's gonna get
away unless I chase the car


00:06:34.147 --> 00:06:35.783
Chase the car!


00:06:53.485 --> 00:06:57.193
Help, help, somebody!


00:06:58.262 --> 00:07:00.600
Hey pal, you gotta help me!


00:07:00.634 --> 00:07:02.270
Please, I can't breathe in here!


00:07:02.303 --> 00:07:04.908
Open it, open it, quick, please!


00:07:05.677 --> 00:07:06.579
It doesn't open!


00:07:08.215 --> 00:07:10.286
Maybe we could ask the
police officer for help?


00:07:10.319 --> 00:07:13.158
Are you nuts?


00:07:13.192 --> 00:07:16.431
Here, let me try.


00:07:38.007 --> 00:07:41.114
No, no, please, no,
no not in there.


00:07:43.218 --> 00:07:46.324
Ow no, no, please
look, look, can we,


00:07:49.063 --> 00:07:54.073
I can't do, I choke, I, I
can't breathe, no, it's just


00:07:54.742 --> 00:07:56.679
no, no, no, no, no, not there!


00:07:59.417 --> 00:08:00.252
Help!


00:08:21.729 --> 00:08:23.030
Oh jeepers, oh jeepers,


00:08:24.167 --> 00:08:25.637
what kind of horrible
place is, hold on.


00:08:33.151 --> 00:08:33.786
What the?


00:08:44.575 --> 00:08:48.750
Teach you to mess
with my masterpiece.


00:08:48.783 --> 00:08:51.087
W- hat did you
just, who are you?


00:08:51.121 --> 00:08:55.730
Some call me the
Dark Feline, others,


00:08:55.764 --> 00:08:57.400
the Un-Collared crusader!


00:08:58.836 --> 00:09:01.241
But all tremble before the
hero Glenfield deserves.


00:09:03.278 --> 00:09:04.113
Turbocat!


00:09:06.652 --> 00:09:07.888
A cat?


00:09:07.921 --> 00:09:10.225
I should have known.


00:09:10.259 --> 00:09:11.528
Bark, bark blah blah blah.


00:09:11.561 --> 00:09:12.831
Ha, it's my nap time.


00:09:13.866 --> 00:09:15.670
Turbocat is out of here.


00:09:41.889 --> 00:09:44.595
Smokescreen.


00:09:56.952 --> 00:09:58.623
You danged kids!


00:09:58.656 --> 00:09:59.825
Too easy!


00:09:59.858 --> 00:10:01.796
Activate autopilot.


00:10:01.829 --> 00:10:02.898
Update status.


00:10:03.866 --> 00:10:07.306
Turbocat sticks it
to the humans again.


00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:09.845
Hashtag: Stupid mutts!


00:10:09.878 --> 00:10:11.481
Hashtag: Awesome!


00:10:34.862 --> 00:10:36.564
Welcome home sir,


00:10:36.598 --> 00:10:39.470
and might I say you were
especially heroic tonight.


00:10:39.504 --> 00:10:42.476
Shame some dumb mutt
tried to abuse my artwork.


00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.846
We should celebrate sir,


00:10:43.880 --> 00:10:46.752
but I'm terribly sorry,
we're fresh out of milk.


00:10:47.921 --> 00:10:49.557
Nah, later, Sinclair.


00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:51.996
I'm too worn out being
awesome to drink now anyway.


00:10:57.974 --> 00:10:58.976
Ahhhhh, nap time.


00:11:08.796 --> 00:11:09.898
Hey, let me out!


00:11:09.932 --> 00:11:11.936
Hey, will you can it!


00:11:11.969 --> 00:11:14.574
If my nap time gets ruined
by some stupid stray dog!


00:11:16.044 --> 00:11:16.946
I'm not a stray!


00:11:16.979 --> 00:11:18.916
I was fired into space in 1969!


00:11:20.586 --> 00:11:22.022
Yeah, right!


00:11:22.056 --> 00:11:23.893
And I walked on the moon
in my pajamas last weekend.


00:11:23.926 --> 00:11:25.629
Of course you're a stray.


00:11:26.966 --> 00:11:28.535
Connect to the CCTV network.


00:11:30.072 --> 00:11:33.011
Isolate the dog's barking
and scan backwards.


00:11:43.064 --> 00:11:44.201
See?


00:11:44.234 --> 00:11:47.106
You're a dirty old stray.


00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.884
But since you're
clearly new round here


00:11:52.918 --> 00:11:54.922
I'll give you the 101.


00:11:54.955 --> 00:11:59.130
You're in Glenfield,
where humans hate animals.


00:12:00.599 --> 00:12:05.108
And when Officer Peck finds
a dangerous unhygienic stray


00:12:05.142 --> 00:12:06.779
animal he locks
them up in the pound


00:12:06.812 --> 00:12:10.152
and they're never seen again.


00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.693
Close the door on your way out.


00:12:13.726 --> 00:12:16.865
Yeah, well, I hope you
get sent to the pound!


00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.807
I'm not gonna though.


00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:23.044
- Know why?
- Uh...


00:12:24.046 --> 00:12:25.216
Because I've got one of these.


00:12:25.249 --> 00:12:27.586
Oh!


00:12:27.619 --> 00:12:28.255
And that.


00:12:32.596 --> 00:12:34.500
This, that, that, this,


00:12:38.209 --> 00:12:39.010
two of those


00:12:41.614 --> 00:12:42.217
and this.


00:12:46.124 --> 00:12:47.861
Triple ply carbon fiber.


00:12:47.894 --> 00:12:49.163
Hand stitched.


00:12:49.197 --> 00:12:52.169
As worn by Glenfield's uncatchable
and incredibly handsome


00:12:52.203 --> 00:12:55.977
super cat, sticking
it to the humans 24/7.


00:12:57.213 --> 00:12:58.014
Ah, ah!


00:12:58.048 --> 00:13:01.120
Don't touch the cape.


00:13:02.189 --> 00:13:04.060
Um, there does appear to be


00:13:04.093 --> 00:13:07.099
a little UHT remaining,
Master Felix Sir.


00:13:07.132 --> 00:13:11.308
Ugh, how many times
it's a secret identity.


00:13:12.676 --> 00:13:14.146
You met Sinclair already.


00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:16.117
80's technology
but I fixed him up


00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:19.391
to be my loyal companion
and open cans of cat food.


00:13:23.766 --> 00:13:26.037
Oh geez, I'm lost 50 years
in the future in a town


00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:29.043
where everyone hates animals,
and the only other pet


00:13:29.076 --> 00:13:32.082
is some kind of
crazy-super-cat-thingy.


00:13:33.118 --> 00:13:35.756
I hope David comes to
find me real quick!


00:13:37.092 --> 00:13:38.329
What?


00:13:38.362 --> 00:13:41.000
Don't tell me you're
drooling over a human


00:13:41.033 --> 00:13:42.403
Careful, cat.


00:13:42.437 --> 00:13:45.041
David loved me so
much he fired me off


00:13:45.075 --> 00:13:47.112
in an experimental
space capsule!


00:13:48.983 --> 00:13:50.185
Oh, he sounds great.


00:13:50.219 --> 00:13:55.162
I mean, maybe if you can find
this so-called space capsule


00:13:56.265 --> 00:13:58.168
this so-called animal
lover will come


00:13:58.201 --> 00:14:00.205
and find his
so-called moron dog!


00:14:01.275 --> 00:14:02.209
That's it!


00:14:02.243 --> 00:14:04.814
David said he'd come
and find the capsule.


00:14:04.848 --> 00:14:07.019
He can't find me
if I'm not with it!


00:14:08.989 --> 00:14:10.192
But how's a little doggie


00:14:10.226 --> 00:14:11.361
like me gonna find
a space capsule?


00:14:13.164 --> 00:14:17.039
- OK, maybe I wasn't clear
before: you're a butt sniffing,


00:14:17.072 --> 00:14:18.309
drool dispensing doofus


00:14:18.342 --> 00:14:19.978
and I'm not gonna help you find


00:14:20.011 --> 00:14:22.984
a space whatnot
or a nasty human.


00:14:24.821 --> 00:14:27.059
OK, you leave me no choice.


00:14:34.341 --> 00:14:37.280
What are you doing?


00:14:37.313 --> 00:14:40.118
Trying to show
you that I'm nice?


00:14:40.151 --> 00:14:42.824
This usually works on humans.


00:14:42.857 --> 00:14:45.263
I'm sick of
hearing about humans.


00:14:45.296 --> 00:14:46.130
Sinclair!


00:14:48.067 --> 00:14:48.902
Wait, wait!


00:14:51.341 --> 00:14:52.477
Maybe if you had some milk


00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:54.179
I'd have listened to you.


00:14:54.213 --> 00:14:58.255
Laters.


00:15:09.611 --> 00:15:11.315
Ugh!


00:15:28.615 --> 00:15:32.557
Oh boy, I hope spacesuits
aren't dry-clean only.


00:15:36.665 --> 00:15:41.173
Ah jeepers, when did humans
get so mean to animals?


00:15:42.343 --> 00:15:43.612
David wasn't like that.


00:15:45.081 --> 00:15:45.916
He loved animals.


00:15:47.085 --> 00:15:47.987
Now all I've got
to remember him by


00:15:48.020 --> 00:15:49.256
is this packed lunch he left me.


00:15:59.276 --> 00:16:03.285
Yeah, thing is, I
only drink full fat.


00:16:05.489 --> 00:16:08.027
Oh gee whiz mister
Felix Turbocat sir,


00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:11.233
you got to help me find
the space capsule, please.


00:16:11.267 --> 00:16:14.307
I found the hatch
already, this was there.


00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:15.376
Sinclair, fetch a camera


00:16:15.409 --> 00:16:18.615
so I can film myself
kicking his butt this time.


00:16:20.018 --> 00:16:23.257
You're my only hope
to find David, please.


00:16:23.291 --> 00:16:26.063
Ugh, you're still chasing
after that dumb human, huh?


00:16:28.368 --> 00:16:31.441
David might be a
human but I believe,


00:16:31.475 --> 00:16:34.481
deep in my heart,
that humans are good,


00:16:35.649 --> 00:16:37.487
and that David's out there


00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:38.689
looking for me right now.


00:16:40.158 --> 00:16:43.264
Please, will you use
your powers to help me


00:16:43.297 --> 00:16:45.569
so I can be reunited
with my owner


00:16:45.603 --> 00:16:48.074
as their loyal, loving pet.


00:16:50.779 --> 00:16:51.816
Huh?


00:16:51.849 --> 00:16:54.119
Sorry, can you summarize that?


00:16:55.489 --> 00:16:56.324
Er, woof?


00:16:57.259 --> 00:16:59.631
Awww, the little
doggy hasn't realized.


00:16:59.664 --> 00:17:02.503
This David isn't
coming to find you


00:17:02.537 --> 00:17:06.344
because humans hate animals.


00:17:09.350 --> 00:17:12.356
Oh geez, I'm I'm sorry
I wasted your time.


00:17:50.298 --> 00:17:54.875
Sir, the bite marks on this
carrot are highly familiar.


00:17:56.645 --> 00:17:59.249
Huh, hit up the CCTV again.


00:18:07.868 --> 00:18:10.539
That one, full screen.


00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:13.445
Top left.


00:18:14.915 --> 00:18:15.749
Zoom in.


00:18:16.651 --> 00:18:17.888
Closer, stop!


00:18:17.921 --> 00:18:19.390
Enhance.


00:18:23.598 --> 00:18:24.434
Cassidy.


00:18:27.039 --> 00:18:27.941
You're right sir!


00:18:27.974 --> 00:18:29.377
Perhaps Ms. Cassidy knows


00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:32.550
the whereabouts of this
alleged space capsule?


00:18:33.752 --> 00:18:35.957
Rabbit has my space capsule?


00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.493
I love chasing rabbits!


00:18:37.526 --> 00:18:39.363
So do I, so do I.


00:18:42.938 --> 00:18:46.845
Yeah, well, er, since I've got
nothing planned I reckon I'll


00:18:46.879 --> 00:18:48.448
take a look around,


00:18:48.482 --> 00:18:50.586
see if I can work out
where she's hiding.


00:18:54.393 --> 00:18:55.462
Sinclair, get the car.


00:18:55.496 --> 00:18:58.068
Shall I pack some lettuce
for Ms. Cassidy, sir?


00:18:58.101 --> 00:19:01.608
Yeah, let's make
it cozy in there.


00:19:01.641 --> 00:19:02.676
Does this mean I
can come with you?


00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:05.516
Turbocat works
alone, dog breath!


00:19:09.023 --> 00:19:11.494
Confirm stray
animals in the park.


00:19:12.530 --> 00:19:14.600
Sinclair, the car?


00:19:22.583 --> 00:19:24.821
What do we do now, Felix?


00:19:24.854 --> 00:19:25.689
Felix?


00:19:26.724 --> 00:19:29.497
Felix!


00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:31.501
Hey, wait for me!


00:19:32.636 --> 00:19:34.841
Hey, don't run
with me you idiot!


00:19:34.874 --> 00:19:38.415
Run the other way!


00:19:40.853 --> 00:19:42.056
But if I run another way


00:19:42.089 --> 00:19:44.627
he won't be able to
chase both of us!


00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:45.964
Ugh, stupid dog!


00:19:47.666 --> 00:19:48.501
Here, fetch!


00:19:52.476 --> 00:19:53.678
You dropped this!


00:19:53.712 --> 00:19:54.379
It's really fun to
catch it though.


00:19:54.413 --> 00:19:57.152
Do you want to drop it again?


00:19:57.186 --> 00:20:00.659
Unbelievable.


00:20:13.184 --> 00:20:14.020
Help me David!


00:20:18.862 --> 00:20:19.697
What the?


00:20:20.866 --> 00:20:22.569
What did you just?


00:20:22.603 --> 00:20:23.571
Do it again!


00:20:32.623 --> 00:20:34.794
How are you doing that?


00:20:34.827 --> 00:20:37.666
I don't know, I don't know!


00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:38.735
Well keep doing it!


00:20:38.768 --> 00:20:43.745
Don't stop!


00:20:57.606 --> 00:20:58.976
I'm coming David!


00:20:59.010 --> 00:20:59.910
I'm coming!


00:21:31.774 --> 00:21:34.713
You need to work on stopping.


00:21:34.747 --> 00:21:38.721
Sorry Felix, I'm just excited
I'm on the trail of David.


00:21:38.755 --> 00:21:42.663
I told you it's
Turbocat, oh, forget it.


00:21:42.696 --> 00:21:44.800
Ugh, I can't believe
I'm gonna have


00:21:44.834 --> 00:21:47.639
to find Cassidy without my cape.


00:21:47.673 --> 00:21:50.679
Look, I don't know how you
did that running thing,


00:21:50.712 --> 00:21:53.785
like you've had too much
marrowbone jelly or something


00:21:53.818 --> 00:21:56.023
but I guess it could
come in useful.


00:21:56.992 --> 00:21:59.663
How do I know I can trust you?


00:21:59.697 --> 00:22:01.167
You shot me already!


00:22:01.200 --> 00:22:04.807
Plus cats do that
licking thing, yuck.


00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:06.777
One word: hy-giene.


00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:09.884
My name's Buddy, not Gene!


00:22:09.917 --> 00:22:11.854
And I still don't know
if I can trust you!


00:22:11.888 --> 00:22:12.789
Who is this Cassidy?


00:22:12.823 --> 00:22:14.260
Where are we anyway?


00:22:17.466 --> 00:22:20.473
That carrot you found
came from this store,


00:22:20.506 --> 00:22:22.676
so it's odds-on this
is she's hiding.


00:22:23.912 --> 00:22:26.485
They don't open for an hour,
but we need to be careful.


00:22:26.518 --> 00:22:27.319
Come on.


00:22:32.429 --> 00:22:33.932
Every time!


00:22:33.965 --> 00:22:35.235
Coast is clear, eugh!


00:22:37.806 --> 00:22:39.210
I think you got
some drool on me.


00:22:39.243 --> 00:22:41.814
Eugh the smell,
it'll never come off.


00:22:45.222 --> 00:22:47.826
Jeepers, I've never seen
a store this big before.


00:22:48.795 --> 00:22:49.797
Ooh look, a ball!


00:22:58.881 --> 00:23:00.051
OK it's a really bouncy ball


00:23:00.085 --> 00:23:01.220
but I nearly got it and there
some others too that I saw


00:23:01.254 --> 00:23:02.289
but I didn't chase.


00:23:03.157 --> 00:23:04.426
- What?
- Nothing.


00:23:05.630 --> 00:23:08.234
There is absolutely nothing
idiotic about this behavior.


00:23:08.268 --> 00:23:10.905
Oh, okay, good,
because for a, bubbles!


00:23:18.888 --> 00:23:19.724
I think I got all of them but


00:23:19.758 --> 00:23:21.827
if you see any more
let me know, OK?


00:23:21.861 --> 00:23:23.565
It is at the top
of my to do list.


00:23:23.599 --> 00:23:25.902
Great, I'll look out for, car!


00:23:29.511 --> 00:23:31.380
It's a lot smaller
than I thought!


00:23:32.282 --> 00:23:33.885
Tastes funny too.


00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:41.867
OK, I can deal
with the drooling


00:23:41.901 --> 00:23:43.639
and I'm prepared to look
away if you want to sniff


00:23:43.672 --> 00:23:46.611
another dog's butt,
but there are limits!


00:23:49.983 --> 00:23:51.354
So you want one too, Felix?


00:23:53.157 --> 00:23:57.032
Felix?


00:23:57.065 --> 00:23:57.899
Felix?


00:23:58.935 --> 00:23:59.970
I'm napping.


00:24:00.939 --> 00:24:02.042
But we're in a hurry.


00:24:02.075 --> 00:24:02.909
Sorry.


00:24:02.943 --> 00:24:04.079
Napping.


00:24:04.113 --> 00:24:04.947
Sunbeam.


00:24:07.352 --> 00:24:08.988
Hey, wake up.


00:24:09.021 --> 00:24:10.693
I need you to help me
find my capsule and David.


00:24:10.726 --> 00:24:12.229
Remember?


00:24:12.262 --> 00:24:13.665
And I'm napping,


00:24:13.699 --> 00:24:17.038
and don't give two hoots about
your dumb human, remember?


00:24:18.609 --> 00:24:22.014
Er, I had actually
forgotten that, but geez,


00:24:22.048 --> 00:24:24.386
I heard cats were
lazy, I didn't realize


00:24:24.420 --> 00:24:26.490
they were this selfish too.


00:24:26.524 --> 00:24:27.526
OK, that's it.


00:24:27.560 --> 00:24:28.361
I'm out of here.


00:24:29.731 --> 00:24:31.467
I can find Cassidy myself
without this hassle


00:24:32.770 --> 00:24:35.007
and without getting
dog hair on everything.


00:24:35.041 --> 00:24:36.343
Huh?


00:24:36.377 --> 00:24:37.212
No, come back!


00:24:50.037 --> 00:24:52.007
Oh, you criminal genius.


00:24:55.281 --> 00:24:56.317
It's locked.


00:24:56.350 --> 00:24:57.553
We'll have to go outside


00:24:57.587 --> 00:24:58.789
and come all the
way back in again.


00:24:58.822 --> 00:25:00.425
Like I don't have
better things to...


00:25:05.603 --> 00:25:06.671
Dang it, a human!


00:25:08.474 --> 00:25:09.711
And we're trapped in here.


00:25:09.744 --> 00:25:12.783
Brilliant.


00:25:12.817 --> 00:25:15.455
Her bike's jamming the door!


00:25:15.488 --> 00:25:17.693
She just needs to get
on it and ride off


00:25:17.727 --> 00:25:18.729
for crying out loud.


00:25:19.764 --> 00:25:20.699
Hey, kid!


00:25:20.733 --> 00:25:22.603
Go home, scram!


00:25:25.375 --> 00:25:28.715
Yeah, I'm way
bigger than I look!


00:25:28.749 --> 00:25:32.522
My hissing signals
immanent violence!


00:25:34.761 --> 00:25:36.230
Dang it, this normally works!


00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:41.273
Ah Felix, I think
she's afraid of us.


00:25:41.307 --> 00:25:43.679
We've got to show
her she we're good.


00:25:43.712 --> 00:25:46.250
Like this!


00:25:46.283 --> 00:25:49.891
Haven't you learned,
that doesn't work!


00:25:49.924 --> 00:25:51.628
Well it's the only
thing we've got!


00:25:51.661 --> 00:25:53.665
Give it a chance, please Felix!


00:25:55.836 --> 00:25:56.871
Come on, come on!


00:25:56.905 --> 00:25:59.644
Glenfield police,
officer Peck speaking.


00:26:02.783 --> 00:26:03.619
Hello?


00:26:07.927 --> 00:26:09.162
Hello?


00:26:41.293 --> 00:26:43.632
I just realized I
haven't eaten for 50 years!


00:26:45.601 --> 00:26:48.608
Now I understand why
dogs get tied up outside.


00:26:49.777 --> 00:26:51.246
You could be more discerning.


00:26:54.519 --> 00:26:55.856
What is that incredible smell?


00:26:57.325 --> 00:26:58.461
Agh, don't get DROOL on it!


00:27:02.970 --> 00:27:06.945
Here.


00:27:06.978 --> 00:27:07.980
Purple packaging.


00:27:09.316 --> 00:27:10.953
Anything in purple
is high class.


00:27:10.986 --> 00:27:12.489
Wowzers!


00:27:12.522 --> 00:27:14.559
It never seems to matter
what flavor the can says,


00:27:14.593 --> 00:27:16.731
pet food always tastes the same.


00:27:17.900 --> 00:27:20.404
Ha ha, ain't that the truth.


00:27:23.043 --> 00:27:26.785
So, that was a neat trick
you pulled on the human.


00:27:26.818 --> 00:27:28.855
Oh it wasn't a trick.


00:27:28.889 --> 00:27:31.661
I knew humans still
loved animals!


00:27:31.694 --> 00:27:34.967
Yeah, my experience of humans


00:27:35.001 --> 00:27:37.338
is clearly radically
different from yours.


00:27:37.372 --> 00:27:39.609
When Peck came to town he
told all the other humans


00:27:39.644 --> 00:27:41.881
that animals were
mean and dangerous


00:27:41.915 --> 00:27:43.852
and then locked
up all the strays.


00:27:45.087 --> 00:27:48.127
And is that when you started
dressing up as TurboCat?


00:27:48.161 --> 00:27:50.699
Hey, hey, it's
not dressing up!


00:27:50.732 --> 00:27:51.968
And what's with that get-up?


00:27:52.001 --> 00:27:53.404
You don't actually


00:27:53.437 --> 00:27:55.408
expect me to believe
you went into space?


00:27:55.441 --> 00:27:56.845
Sure I did!


00:27:56.878 --> 00:27:58.949
They trained a whole
load of animals,


00:27:58.982 --> 00:28:02.455
rabbits, dogs, mice, even a cat.


00:28:02.488 --> 00:28:04.092
But David picked me.


00:28:04.125 --> 00:28:07.532
He said his own pet was the
one he trusted most of all.


00:28:07.565 --> 00:28:10.104
What, and you
just believed him?


00:28:10.137 --> 00:28:11.774
Of course!


00:28:11.808 --> 00:28:16.751
I told you, I believe
deep down humans are good.


00:28:22.562 --> 00:28:24.099
Freeze!


00:28:24.132 --> 00:28:24.934
You want to test
that hypothesis?


00:28:24.967 --> 00:28:26.503
Uh, maybe later!


00:28:40.666 --> 00:28:42.670
We have you surrounded!


00:28:42.703 --> 00:28:44.105
Don't try to run!


00:28:44.139 --> 00:28:45.041
Climb!


00:29:19.343 --> 00:29:20.712
Freeze!


00:29:20.746 --> 00:29:22.515
Lower your paws and step
away from the glass!


00:29:24.186 --> 00:29:25.288
Hey, what do you?


00:29:25.322 --> 00:29:27.091
You!


00:29:27.125 --> 00:29:28.294
The so-called Turbocat!


00:29:28.328 --> 00:29:29.562
What is your mission?


00:29:30.966 --> 00:29:32.936
Are you searching for
supplies of catnip again?


00:29:34.606 --> 00:29:35.541
Catnip...


00:29:44.727 --> 00:29:45.929
Cease and desist!


00:29:45.962 --> 00:29:49.069
How did you locate the secret
headquarters of G.U.A.R.D.?


00:29:49.102 --> 00:29:50.338
Er, say what now?


00:29:50.372 --> 00:29:51.207
G.U.A.R.D.


00:29:52.876 --> 00:29:56.183
Glenfield Underground
Animal Rights Division.


00:29:57.319 --> 00:29:59.189
I'm head of Tactical Operations,


00:29:59.223 --> 00:30:02.195
and this is our public
relations specialist: Tinker.


00:30:02.229 --> 00:30:04.099
Er, Bullion, if these
neutrino readings are accura...


00:30:04.132 --> 00:30:05.836
Not now, Tinker!


00:30:05.869 --> 00:30:07.840
Hey, now I've just about had...


00:30:07.873 --> 00:30:09.042
Silence!


00:30:09.075 --> 00:30:13.183
Remain in your present positions
or you will be neutralized.


00:30:13.218 --> 00:30:14.253
At ease Bullion!


00:30:15.755 --> 00:30:18.928
I'll tell you if I need
anyone neutralizing.


00:30:21.133 --> 00:30:22.068
Ma'am yes ma'am.


00:30:22.101 --> 00:30:23.738
Commencing perimeter patrol!


00:30:28.748 --> 00:30:29.984
Cassidy!


00:30:30.017 --> 00:30:32.155
F-fancy running into you!


00:30:43.745 --> 00:30:47.118
Confirm stray animals
located at Mega Store.


00:30:47.151 --> 00:30:49.957
- Proceeding to investigate.
- 10-4.


00:30:51.427 --> 00:30:53.965
Congratulations Felix,


00:30:53.998 --> 00:30:56.971
you've led Peck RIGHT
to our secret hideout.


00:30:57.004 --> 00:30:59.042
Now we need a new place to hide.


00:31:01.414 --> 00:31:03.116
I thought you'd never ask.


00:31:05.322 --> 00:31:06.924
It's lovely to see
you again Ms. Cassidy.


00:31:06.958 --> 00:31:09.496
Can I offer you
some spring water?


00:31:09.530 --> 00:31:11.801
You always did
serve the best, Sinc'.


00:31:13.371 --> 00:31:15.174
Yeah, I upgraded
him since last time.


00:31:15.207 --> 00:31:18.146
Two terabytes storage and
he does sparkling and still.


00:31:18.180 --> 00:31:19.283
Ms. Cassidy,


00:31:20.518 --> 00:31:22.856
Felix told me that you could
help me find my space capsule.


00:31:22.889 --> 00:31:26.162
Actually, we hoped you
could help us find it.


00:31:26.196 --> 00:31:27.799
Sinclair, if you would.


00:31:33.243 --> 00:31:35.214
8K high definition video
streaming in realtime.


00:31:35.247 --> 00:31:37.286
Pretty awesome, huh?


00:31:37.319 --> 00:31:38.921
Thank you Felix.


00:31:40.358 --> 00:31:43.498
As you know Buddy, in 1969
you were selected from a group


00:31:43.531 --> 00:31:47.539
of highly trained animals to
fly in an experimental rocket.


00:31:48.508 --> 00:31:50.210
David!


00:31:50.244 --> 00:31:52.181
But what you don't know
is that the space capsule


00:31:52.214 --> 00:31:53.216
was secretly powered


00:31:53.250 --> 00:31:57.191
by a crystalline substance
called hyperlithium.


00:32:00.197 --> 00:32:02.101
There was a crystal
in the space capsule?


00:32:02.134 --> 00:32:04.238
But I just thought
it was a rocket!


00:32:05.642 --> 00:32:07.346
Double rocket powered,
and with titanium chassis,


00:32:07.379 --> 00:32:10.418
ejection seats and
check this out.


00:32:12.054 --> 00:32:13.291
Quiet please Felix.


00:32:14.493 --> 00:32:17.332
Buddy, G.U.A.R.D.'s mission
is to find the space capsule


00:32:17.366 --> 00:32:20.070
and use the
Hyperlithium to protect


00:32:20.104 --> 00:32:22.409
the animals of Glenfield.


00:32:22.442 --> 00:32:24.413
But how can a crystal help?


00:32:25.982 --> 00:32:28.354
Erm, the Hyperlithium
emits energy waves that can...


00:32:28.388 --> 00:32:30.692
That's
a good question!


00:32:39.309 --> 00:32:43.150
Buddy, our chief
scientist, Todd.


00:32:43.183 --> 00:32:44.953
It's an honor!


00:32:44.987 --> 00:32:47.224
And to answer your question


00:32:47.258 --> 00:32:48.961
this little invention of mine


00:32:48.995 --> 00:32:52.067
is powered by only
a tiny crystal.


00:32:55.007 --> 00:32:56.343
Once we've found
the space capsule,


00:32:56.377 --> 00:32:58.448
we'll harness the Hyperlithium


00:32:58.481 --> 00:33:02.656
to power a much larger
machine, GUARDIAN!


00:33:05.328 --> 00:33:06.464
Oh golly!


00:33:07.466 --> 00:33:08.701
With GUARDIAN, the
animals of Glenfield


00:33:08.734 --> 00:33:11.540
will finally be able
to stand up to Peck.


00:33:12.742 --> 00:33:14.346
We have to find
the space capsule!


00:33:14.379 --> 00:33:15.982
It's our only hope.


00:33:36.323 --> 00:33:41.065
As you can see we're having
some teething troubles.


00:33:42.234 --> 00:33:45.375
Buddy, will you join
G.U.A.R.D. and help us?


00:33:47.512 --> 00:33:50.718
He's gonna fit right in
with the rest of those losers!


00:33:52.121 --> 00:33:55.461
Felix, remind me
how TurboCat pays


00:33:55.495 --> 00:33:58.401
for all the gadgets
and capes and so on?


00:34:09.356 --> 00:34:12.462
160 million views.


00:34:12.495 --> 00:34:15.602
The advertising
royalties must be super.


00:34:24.553 --> 00:34:26.357
Hey, that one's not funny!


00:34:26.390 --> 00:34:29.295
No one can resist the
spot of light, OK?


00:34:35.375 --> 00:34:39.750
Buddy, Felix wants me to
come live in his secret base


00:34:39.783 --> 00:34:41.487
and play with all
his super-gadgets


00:34:41.520 --> 00:34:44.493
but I believe we can
free Glenfield's animals


00:34:44.526 --> 00:34:48.601
from Peck's tyranny if
we all work together.


00:34:50.471 --> 00:34:52.575
Er, I'm just a dog.


00:34:52.609 --> 00:34:54.881
You're an animal hero, Buddy.


00:34:57.352 --> 00:34:58.319
And we need heroes.


00:35:02.395 --> 00:35:03.263
It worked!


00:35:03.296 --> 00:35:05.300
I've got a vector
on the Hyperlithium!


00:35:05.333 --> 00:35:07.405
Er, connecting to
the CCTV network now!


00:35:10.343 --> 00:35:11.881
We're too late.


00:35:11.915 --> 00:35:15.421
Peck has found the capsule and
taken it back to the pound!


00:35:15.455 --> 00:35:19.228
No pet has ever gone
in and come out again!


00:35:20.631 --> 00:35:21.467
Ahem.


00:35:23.336 --> 00:35:24.941
This sounds like a
job for Turbocat!


00:36:01.513 --> 00:36:03.784
Hey Cassidy, mission,


00:36:03.818 --> 00:36:06.355
Turbocat-gets-capsule,
phase one completed!


00:36:07.125 --> 00:36:08.494
Felix you idiot!


00:36:08.527 --> 00:36:10.464
You're gonna get us all caught!


00:36:10.498 --> 00:36:11.099
Get back here this minute...


00:36:12.068 --> 00:36:13.437
Yeah, I thought so too.


00:36:13.470 --> 00:36:15.340
Proceeding to phase two, huh?


00:36:32.442 --> 00:36:34.112
It's almost too easy.


00:36:45.468 --> 00:36:49.709
The space capsule is
right behind this door.


00:36:57.025 --> 00:36:58.627
You're not a space capsule!


00:36:58.661 --> 00:37:01.033
Hey, hey, are you
here to get me out!


00:37:01.066 --> 00:37:02.735
Please, help, come on!


00:37:03.837 --> 00:37:05.541
I must have
taken a wrong turn.


00:37:05.574 --> 00:37:07.645
Hey, get me outta here!


00:37:07.679 --> 00:37:10.084
I can't breathe in
this place, please!


00:37:11.286 --> 00:37:13.090
Hey be quie, Peck
is right down the...


00:37:13.123 --> 00:37:14.626
Arrggh!


00:37:14.659 --> 00:37:15.528
What the?


00:37:15.561 --> 00:37:17.732
Get it off, get it off!


00:37:17.765 --> 00:37:19.703
- Sorry!
- Dang it!


00:37:19.736 --> 00:37:20.771
Shut up!


00:37:25.147 --> 00:37:27.885
Will you cut it out with that?


00:37:29.756 --> 00:37:31.693
Danged thing won't...


00:37:40.177 --> 00:37:41.680
Because I can hear it
barking right down the hall,


00:37:41.713 --> 00:37:44.152
that's why, it's dangerous!


00:37:45.354 --> 00:37:47.125
And disgusting.


00:37:50.631 --> 00:37:51.600
Hold on, I've got another call.


00:37:51.633 --> 00:37:53.237
Hello?


00:37:53.270 --> 00:37:54.172
Hello?


00:37:54.205 --> 00:37:55.976
James, it's your father here.


00:37:56.009 --> 00:37:58.747
Ah, Dad, I'm at work.


00:37:59.682 --> 00:38:01.219
I can't
find my danged radio.


00:38:01.253 --> 00:38:03.257
Well where did
you have it last?


00:38:03.290 --> 00:38:06.329
Well I
was in the bathroom


00:38:06.363 --> 00:38:07.165
and I thought I put it there.


00:38:12.809 --> 00:38:14.813
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
okay, I get the picture.


00:38:16.216 --> 00:38:17.819
I tell you that darn thing
is like 50 years old.


00:38:23.363 --> 00:38:25.101
We can let this guy
out later, come on!


00:38:26.369 --> 00:38:29.977
Hold on, this thing's
still on the blink.


00:38:30.945 --> 00:38:32.348
How'd that happen?


00:38:33.884 --> 00:38:34.686
Follow me!


00:38:36.156 --> 00:38:37.658
Wait up!


00:38:37.692 --> 00:38:40.231
So, er, did Cassidy send you?


00:38:40.264 --> 00:38:42.135
She said something
about a massive jerk


00:38:42.168 --> 00:38:44.739
who deserves to have his
hind kicked for eternity,


00:38:44.772 --> 00:38:48.280
and there were some other words
too but I didn't understand.


00:38:49.149 --> 00:38:50.818
Ah.


00:38:50.851 --> 00:38:53.423
But we've got to get the
capsule, now more than ever!


00:38:53.457 --> 00:38:54.292
This way!


00:39:02.241 --> 00:39:03.243
There it is!


00:39:05.515 --> 00:39:06.750
Hold up!


00:39:11.527 --> 00:39:12.361
Slow down!


00:39:28.995 --> 00:39:29.829
Whoa!


00:39:45.928 --> 00:39:46.896
What the what?


00:40:00.190 --> 00:40:03.096
Do you have any idea what
they're gonna do to us?


00:40:04.399 --> 00:40:05.602
Take us somewhere nice


00:40:05.635 --> 00:40:08.140
where there's plenty
of food and sunbeams?


00:40:08.173 --> 00:40:12.448
No, someplace where I won't
be able to breathe at all!


00:40:14.218 --> 00:40:15.254
Geez Felix.


00:40:16.423 --> 00:40:19.195
How was I to know your high-tech
multi-function cat blaster


00:40:19.228 --> 00:40:21.966
was so sensitive?


00:40:22.000 --> 00:40:22.602
I'm sorry.


00:40:23.470 --> 00:40:25.207
Ah, it's not your fault.


00:40:26.376 --> 00:40:29.015
It's the sort of mistake
anyone could make.


00:40:30.652 --> 00:40:33.223
I just really needed
to see David again.


00:40:33.256 --> 00:40:37.566
He's always been there for
me, ever since I was a puppy.


00:40:39.235 --> 00:40:41.640
Well, ever since I was a
kitten I've been a stray,


00:40:41.674 --> 00:40:44.345
out on the street, alone.


00:40:44.379 --> 00:40:46.883
I never had anyone who
looked out for me like that.


00:40:47.985 --> 00:40:49.922
Thanks for trying to rescue me.


00:40:51.059 --> 00:40:53.029
It was pretty heroic.


00:40:55.401 --> 00:41:00.009
So is this a
normal day at work, Dad?


00:41:01.146 --> 00:41:04.152
No, I only go to
headquarters once a month.


00:41:04.185 --> 00:41:06.089
And on a normal day childcare


00:41:06.122 --> 00:41:08.025
doesn't cancel at
the last minute.


00:41:09.027 --> 00:41:11.299
What is that thing, Dad?


00:41:11.332 --> 00:41:13.671
Dangerous,
you leave that to me.


00:41:16.342 --> 00:41:20.552
And are the animals
really dangerous too, Dad?


00:41:20.585 --> 00:41:21.587
The strays?


00:41:22.789 --> 00:41:25.562
They're filthy, they
could have diseases,


00:41:25.595 --> 00:41:29.101
and Alex, you know you
can't ever trust an animal.


00:41:29.135 --> 00:41:29.736
Yeah, but...


00:41:29.770 --> 00:41:31.038
But nothing, Alex!


00:41:32.642 --> 00:41:35.012
I just think they're
no good for our town.


00:42:06.209 --> 00:42:06.810
Heads-up.


00:42:06.844 --> 00:42:07.812
Cassidy!


00:42:07.846 --> 00:42:09.783
Whoa, rescue mission!?


00:42:10.852 --> 00:42:12.689
Just like old times, eh Felix?


00:42:12.722 --> 00:42:14.760
You go storming
in all by yourself


00:42:14.793 --> 00:42:17.632
and leave me to
clean up after you.


00:42:17.666 --> 00:42:20.103
Wow, pretty amazing.


00:42:20.137 --> 00:42:21.840
I knew you had some secret moves


00:42:21.874 --> 00:42:23.410
with that thing, abracadabra


00:42:28.219 --> 00:42:31.492
Don't say that again.


00:42:35.668 --> 00:42:37.772
If Todd's aligned the
explosives correctly


00:42:37.806 --> 00:42:42.147
we should be out of here
in three, two, one...


00:43:05.394 --> 00:43:06.295
The kid!


00:43:06.329 --> 00:43:06.930
She must still be inside!


00:43:08.299 --> 00:43:09.936
Buddy, Buddy come back!


00:43:12.241 --> 00:43:13.811
Whoa Buddy, we have
to get out of here.


00:43:13.844 --> 00:43:15.414
But the kid's still in there.


00:43:16.917 --> 00:43:20.257
Okay, okay, you're heaviest.


00:43:20.290 --> 00:43:23.631
Hey, I hadn't
eaten for 50 years!


00:43:23.664 --> 00:43:25.902
So stay here
while I go up front.


00:43:44.740 --> 00:43:45.675
It's moving


00:43:45.708 --> 00:43:47.979
Just a few seconds more!


00:43:49.048 --> 00:43:50.450
It's too heavy!


00:43:51.854 --> 00:43:53.556
Come on Buddy!


00:43:53.590 --> 00:43:55.026
You've been into space
for crying out loud!


00:43:55.060 --> 00:43:59.068
You can do this!


00:44:12.896 --> 00:44:13.931
What?


00:44:29.963 --> 00:44:30.798
What?


00:44:32.467 --> 00:44:35.106
Oh!


00:44:38.914 --> 00:44:43.924
Whoops!


00:44:49.836 --> 00:44:51.606
Incredible footage
coming from highway 17 outside


00:44:51.639 --> 00:44:54.980
Glenfield with what
appears to be a dog


00:44:55.013 --> 00:44:57.451
holding a pick-up
truck in the air.


00:44:57.484 --> 00:44:58.921
That the dog
hasn't been identified yet.


00:44:58.954 --> 00:45:00.056
Lifting the vehicle...


00:45:00.090 --> 00:45:02.628
Truly
an incredible dog.


00:45:02.662 --> 00:45:03.731
Over now Sandra in downtown...


00:45:03.764 --> 00:45:06.135
Now the whole world has
seen the capsule on TV,


00:45:06.169 --> 00:45:08.006
David will come find
me any time now!


00:45:09.876 --> 00:45:11.479
Shows a
cat, pulling a child


00:45:11.512 --> 00:45:15.922
out of the truck
completely unharmed.


00:45:15.955 --> 00:45:18.626
Congratulations sir,
there's one human child


00:45:18.661 --> 00:45:19.963
who might not follow
her father's profession.


00:45:19.996 --> 00:45:22.634
Shall we celebrate with
single cream or double?


00:45:25.808 --> 00:45:27.010
That's much better.


00:45:27.044 --> 00:45:29.114
Always happy to help
a fellow animal, Victor.


00:45:29.148 --> 00:45:30.785
Welcome to G.U.A.R.D.


00:45:32.654 --> 00:45:33.924
Uh, everyone?


00:45:41.038 --> 00:45:43.677
No, no, no, not this way!


00:45:43.711 --> 00:45:46.216
Why didn't you leave
them on the road?


00:45:46.249 --> 00:45:48.821
Ma'am, if the humans
enter the perimeter


00:45:48.854 --> 00:45:51.793
I request permission to use
lasers set to disintegrate!


00:45:59.976 --> 00:46:01.112
Er, hey there.


00:46:06.122 --> 00:46:08.059
Hey, cut it out
with the wagging!


00:46:09.061 --> 00:46:10.931
I'm sorry but I can't help it!


00:46:10.965 --> 00:46:12.100
It just has a mind of its own!


00:46:12.134 --> 00:46:15.173
Well watch what you're doing,
it nearly had my eye out!


00:46:15.207 --> 00:46:16.142
I could have been...


00:46:18.012 --> 00:46:19.014
Hey there you two.


00:46:20.050 --> 00:46:24.959
What is happening?


00:46:25.828 --> 00:46:27.030
Oh, I've heard of this!


00:46:27.064 --> 00:46:29.134
Cats do it before they
cough up a hairball.


00:46:30.070 --> 00:46:33.777
That's coughing, you idiot.


00:46:39.222 --> 00:46:40.825
Nice kitty.


00:46:44.232 --> 00:46:45.066
Don't.


00:46:47.238 --> 00:46:48.072
Alex!


00:46:49.174 --> 00:46:51.011
Oh my gosh, are you OK?


00:46:51.045 --> 00:46:52.180
I'm fine, Dad.


00:46:52.215 --> 00:46:54.084
And so are the animals.


00:46:54.118 --> 00:46:55.053
Animals?


00:46:55.086 --> 00:46:56.155
Did they get loose?


00:46:56.188 --> 00:46:57.057
Did they hurt you?


00:46:57.090 --> 00:46:58.427
Where are they?


00:46:58.460 --> 00:46:59.295
They...


00:47:02.100 --> 00:47:03.370
They escaped.


00:47:03.403 --> 00:47:05.006
Must have run off.


00:47:05.039 --> 00:47:07.210
I'm fine though, they
didn't hurt me or anything.


00:47:08.212 --> 00:47:09.681
Oh, oh thank heavens.


00:47:09.716 --> 00:47:12.355
Sorry Alex, after
what happened to you


00:47:12.388 --> 00:47:15.427
when you were little
I'm just so...


00:47:19.502 --> 00:47:22.207
Maybe I should go get
checked out in the hospital.


00:47:56.075 --> 00:47:57.478
I can't nap
watching you do that.


00:47:57.511 --> 00:48:00.451
Oh, sorry Felix,
I'm waiting for David.


00:48:00.484 --> 00:48:02.421
Well, you're freaking me out.


00:48:02.455 --> 00:48:04.259
Are you sure he's coming?


00:48:04.292 --> 00:48:07.230
He fired you into space
for crying out loud.


00:48:07.265 --> 00:48:08.267
What do you mean?


00:48:08.300 --> 00:48:10.337
Silence on deck!


00:48:10.371 --> 00:48:13.277
We are working with
hazardous materials here!


00:48:14.545 --> 00:48:19.221
The Hyperlithium!


00:48:19.255 --> 00:48:22.495
The effect it's had on
Buddy is incredible.


00:48:24.299 --> 00:48:26.201
Probably
phase-aligned neutrinos


00:48:26.235 --> 00:48:27.505
interacting with his DNA...


00:48:27.538 --> 00:48:29.074
What's wrong, Todd?


00:48:29.107 --> 00:48:29.942
Oh...


00:48:31.178 --> 00:48:36.356
The Hyperlithium is emitting
a strange kind of radiation.


00:48:36.389 --> 00:48:41.399
It has the power to
interact with animal DNA,


00:48:42.268 --> 00:48:44.305
destabilizing it, changing it.


00:48:44.339 --> 00:48:46.008
We must be careful.


00:48:48.179 --> 00:48:51.319
Peck knew it was dangerous.


00:48:51.353 --> 00:48:53.255
What was he planning
to do with it?


00:48:55.561 --> 00:48:57.097
You don't think the humans


00:48:57.130 --> 00:49:00.269
plan to use the
Hyperlithium against us?


00:49:00.304 --> 00:49:02.207
Heaven knows what
humans would do


00:49:02.240 --> 00:49:04.912
if they had this kind of power.


00:49:07.083 --> 00:49:08.987
How long before
Guardian is ready?


00:49:09.020 --> 00:49:11.125
Well I still need to
connect the rocket boosters


00:49:11.158 --> 00:49:12.395
and get the guidance online.


00:49:12.428 --> 00:49:14.264
I'm going as fast as I can.


00:49:18.205 --> 00:49:22.046
But maybe Peck's just
worried about his family.


00:49:22.080 --> 00:49:23.550
He doesn't really mean to...


00:49:23.583 --> 00:49:25.387
I had an owner
once too, Buddy.


00:49:25.421 --> 00:49:29.695
I thought he cared
for me, loved me even.


00:49:29.729 --> 00:49:34.939
But he rejected
me, cast me aside,


00:49:35.607 --> 00:49:36.643
forced me to become a stray,


00:49:37.645 --> 00:49:40.417
living on the street,
hiding in the garbage.


00:49:40.451 --> 00:49:42.555
He's right, Peck
locked me in the pound!


00:49:42.588 --> 00:49:45.327
I couldn't move, I
couldn't breathe.


00:49:45.360 --> 00:49:47.163
I ain't never going back.


00:49:47.197 --> 00:49:52.207
The humans could do anything
to us, like David did to you.


00:49:53.075 --> 00:49:55.347
Hey, David is my friend!


00:49:55.380 --> 00:49:56.281
He's good!


00:49:56.316 --> 00:49:58.487
OK OK, now calm down everyone.


00:49:58.520 --> 00:50:03.028
Ma'am, permission
to use nuclear force?


00:50:03.062 --> 00:50:05.434
Can you please all be quiet?!


00:50:09.509 --> 00:50:11.379
I am trying to nap.


00:50:17.358 --> 00:50:21.666
Master Buddy sir, perhaps you
need to take a short stroll?


00:50:21.699 --> 00:50:24.438
Mr. David might already
be in the neighborhood.


00:50:24.472 --> 00:50:25.374
Of course!


00:50:25.407 --> 00:50:27.444
David might be out
there looking for me!


00:50:29.314 --> 00:50:33.490
Master Felix, perhaps some
warm milk might help you nap.


00:50:37.230 --> 00:50:40.470
Why are you always running
around after that jerk, Sinc'?


00:50:40.504 --> 00:50:43.343
Apologies Ms. Cassidy,
my 1980's programming


00:50:43.376 --> 00:50:45.347
is somewhat obsolete.


00:50:45.380 --> 00:50:48.587
In fact, I believe that was
why I was discarded and thrown


00:50:48.620 --> 00:50:51.191
onto the garbage heap.


00:50:51.224 --> 00:50:54.365
Until Master Felix rescued
and repaired me, of course.


00:50:56.201 --> 00:50:59.876
It really was rather
super, Ms. Cassidy.


00:51:04.452 --> 00:51:07.691
We have to learn more
about the Hyperlithium.


00:51:07.725 --> 00:51:08.827
Agreed.


00:51:08.861 --> 00:51:10.697
Peck's still in the hospital.


00:51:10.731 --> 00:51:12.568
I'll go and get the
rest of the equipment.


00:51:12.601 --> 00:51:13.904
I'll be back before dark.


00:51:21.486 --> 00:51:23.423
Er, excuse me?


00:51:23.456 --> 00:51:25.928
I'm sorry, I thought
Sinclair told you.


00:51:25.962 --> 00:51:27.798
To study the
Hyperlithium we thought


00:51:27.831 --> 00:51:30.637
it was best if I slept over.


00:51:32.408 --> 00:51:33.208
Uh...


00:51:33.242 --> 00:51:34.445
That's OK isn't it?


00:51:34.478 --> 00:51:36.616
Er yeah, it's er,
yes, that's fine.


00:51:36.649 --> 00:51:40.357
I mean yeah, totally,
fine.


00:51:40.390 --> 00:51:42.428
Yes, that's, that's fine.


00:51:44.498 --> 00:51:45.299
OK, good.


00:51:47.438 --> 00:51:48.740
I'm sorry, about earlier.


00:51:50.677 --> 00:51:51.679
In the truck I mean.


00:51:53.450 --> 00:51:56.589
It's just, I spent
years in the magic show,


00:51:56.622 --> 00:51:59.528
hiding inside a hat
before I escaped.


00:51:59.562 --> 00:52:02.534
I learned the hard way there's
no such thing as magic.


00:52:04.538 --> 00:52:06.910
Your whole superhero thing,


00:52:06.944 --> 00:52:08.948
it's like you thought
wearing a cape


00:52:08.981 --> 00:52:10.985
would magically
solve everything.


00:52:13.322 --> 00:52:17.464
I'm sorry, I guess
I was trying to...


00:52:17.498 --> 00:52:18.566
Impress me?


00:52:21.338 --> 00:52:24.044
I just thought if I had
all the gadgets and the mask


00:52:24.078 --> 00:52:26.682
then everyone would
think I was cool


00:52:26.716 --> 00:52:29.755
and no one would realize
how much the whole humans


00:52:29.789 --> 00:52:30.892
thing got to me.


00:52:32.027 --> 00:52:35.567
But now, what
you did, and Buddy,


00:52:36.736 --> 00:52:38.506
maybe Peck won't
catch us after all.


00:52:38.540 --> 00:52:41.479
Maybe we're actually
going to win.


00:52:42.380 --> 00:52:44.886
Maybe magic is real after all.


00:52:47.691 --> 00:52:49.128
I'll get the gear.


00:52:49.161 --> 00:52:50.664
You guard the capsule, okay?


00:52:53.904 --> 00:52:55.574
Guard the capsule.


00:52:57.044 --> 00:52:58.713
Guard the capsule...


00:53:07.764 --> 00:53:10.804
Aw jeepers, I thought
David would be here by now.


00:53:11.974 --> 00:53:13.643
He said he'd come
and find the...


00:53:18.152 --> 00:53:21.726
Space capsule.


00:53:21.759 --> 00:53:22.794
Space capsule!


00:53:34.718 --> 00:53:35.654
The capsule, the truck!


00:53:35.687 --> 00:53:36.555
It's getting away!


00:53:36.589 --> 00:53:37.524
What?


00:53:37.557 --> 00:53:38.826
But the capsule's right...


00:53:38.860 --> 00:53:40.463
It must be Peck!


00:53:40.497 --> 00:53:41.934
He's got out the
hospital, he's found


00:53:41.967 --> 00:53:43.703
where the space
capsule is somehow.


00:53:43.736 --> 00:53:44.571
But how?


00:53:46.008 --> 00:53:46.944
Cassidy!


00:53:46.977 --> 00:53:47.744
He must have caught her


00:53:47.778 --> 00:53:49.148
and she's led him back!


00:53:49.181 --> 00:53:50.650
Which way did he take her?


00:53:50.684 --> 00:53:51.719
This way!


00:54:00.603 --> 00:54:01.639
Get in!


00:54:07.217 --> 00:54:08.686
Hey, no drooling!


00:54:08.720 --> 00:54:10.123
I just had this cleaned.


00:54:10.156 --> 00:54:11.692
Where did the truck go?


00:54:11.726 --> 00:54:12.594
Can I open a window?


00:54:12.627 --> 00:54:14.198
Uh, useless.


00:54:14.231 --> 00:54:15.767
Autopilot: locate the truck.


00:54:16.736 --> 00:54:17.871
Ah, what's that flashing?


00:54:17.904 --> 00:54:20.978
Activating smoke screen.


00:54:22.781 --> 00:54:23.583
You idiot!


00:54:23.616 --> 00:54:24.852
Engage autopilot!


00:54:25.887 --> 00:54:27.090
It's headed for the interstate.


00:54:27.124 --> 00:54:29.061
Autopilot: turn
onto route seven.


00:54:29.094 --> 00:54:29.996
Searching for a restaurant


00:54:30.030 --> 00:54:31.098
with that name locally...


00:54:31.132 --> 00:54:31.932
What?


00:54:31.967 --> 00:54:33.636
No, route seven!


00:54:33.669 --> 00:54:34.671
Searching for a carwash


00:54:34.705 --> 00:54:36.275
with that name locally.


00:54:36.308 --> 00:54:37.310
Let me do it!


00:54:40.717 --> 00:54:41.786
Stop doing that!


00:54:44.158 --> 00:54:45.693
Put it back!


00:54:46.362 --> 00:54:47.764
The other one!


00:54:51.172 --> 00:54:52.841
The other other one!


00:55:01.225 --> 00:55:02.727
- The truck!
- My capsule!


00:55:04.031 --> 00:55:05.767
Cassidy!


00:55:07.972 --> 00:55:09.741
Okay, we can stop
them with this.


00:55:12.247 --> 00:55:13.182
Aim for the fender.


00:55:17.891 --> 00:55:19.294
Not the capsule, get the truck!


00:55:19.328 --> 00:55:21.065
Here, let me do that.


00:55:25.707 --> 00:55:27.144
Stop!


00:55:27.177 --> 00:55:29.014
We have to get the capsule!


00:55:29.948 --> 00:55:30.850
What?


00:55:30.884 --> 00:55:31.719
No way, we're closing in.


00:55:35.793 --> 00:55:36.929
Hey, get off, you moron.


00:55:38.332 --> 00:55:40.703
Without the capsule I'll
never see David again!


00:55:40.737 --> 00:55:43.142
Cassidy's heading to
the pound unless I...


00:55:56.536 --> 00:56:00.210
Do you have any idea how
expensive spare parts


00:56:00.243 --> 00:56:01.812
are for one of these?


00:56:01.845 --> 00:56:02.814
There, look!


00:56:10.863 --> 00:56:11.499
Huh?


00:56:15.574 --> 00:56:17.844
But I don't understand.


00:56:17.877 --> 00:56:20.517
It was a decoy!


00:56:20.551 --> 00:56:22.454
Peck just wanted us to chase it!


00:56:22.487 --> 00:56:23.889
But why?


00:56:25.260 --> 00:56:26.195
To get us away from...


00:56:43.095 --> 00:56:45.266
What were you two doing?


00:56:45.300 --> 00:56:46.569
Cassidy!


00:56:46.603 --> 00:56:48.205
I thought Peck had caught you.


00:56:48.239 --> 00:56:49.141
What?


00:56:49.174 --> 00:56:51.178
I can look after myself, Felix.


00:56:51.211 --> 00:56:52.147
Where's Todd?


00:56:52.180 --> 00:56:54.318
He didn't get out in time.


00:56:54.351 --> 00:56:55.587
Victor too.


00:56:55.621 --> 00:56:57.490
Why the heck weren't you...


00:56:59.127 --> 00:57:01.832
Was there a sunbeam, Felix?


00:57:03.336 --> 00:57:04.504
You were napping?


00:57:04.539 --> 00:57:07.210
You kept me awake
with all that guarding.


00:57:07.243 --> 00:57:10.584
Next thing I know you're
chasing the stupid capsule and...


00:57:10.617 --> 00:57:12.987
And you two fell
right into Peck's trap.


00:57:13.022 --> 00:57:18.032
While you're off playing
at superheroes, he's won.


00:57:19.434 --> 00:57:22.240
He's got Victor, and Todd
and the Hyperlithium.


00:57:22.273 --> 00:57:24.044
It's over.


00:57:25.146 --> 00:57:26.515
Negative ma'am,


00:57:26.549 --> 00:57:28.452
we move in a pincer formation,
surround the building


00:57:28.486 --> 00:57:30.323
and neutralize the humans


00:57:30.356 --> 00:57:31.492
with minimal collateral
damage to G.U.A.R.D.


00:57:31.525 --> 00:57:34.331
Bullion, G.U.A.R.D. is a joke!


00:57:35.601 --> 00:57:37.904
You're about as much use in
tactical operations as a fish!


00:57:39.609 --> 00:57:41.546
Our PR mouse never
says anything.


00:57:42.414 --> 00:57:43.215
Uh...


00:57:43.249 --> 00:57:44.685
And our scientist


00:57:44.719 --> 00:57:45.953
is headed to the pound
because none of you clowns


00:57:45.987 --> 00:57:47.658
can actually work together!


00:57:51.599 --> 00:57:53.001
Peck's gonna catch us,


00:57:54.471 --> 00:57:56.709
and we can't just wave a
magic wand to stop him.


00:58:09.201 --> 00:58:12.173
We've got to get
that capsule back!


00:58:21.693 --> 00:58:22.761
Keep quiet.


00:58:22.795 --> 00:58:24.599
And try not to chase anything.


00:58:24.632 --> 00:58:25.667
Oh I won't.


00:58:26.669 --> 00:58:27.605
Can you try not to nap?


00:58:27.638 --> 00:58:29.709
Oh, so it's my fault!


00:58:29.742 --> 00:58:30.911
None of this would have happened


00:58:30.944 --> 00:58:34.317
if you hadn't gone chasing
after the first thing you see!


00:58:34.351 --> 00:58:36.188
Jumping jeepers,
you were napping


00:58:36.221 --> 00:58:38.459
when you should have been
guarding the capsule!


00:58:39.327 --> 00:58:43.269
There was a sunbeam!


00:58:47.243 --> 00:58:47.811
Peck!


00:58:49.615 --> 00:58:51.853
He better not be
playing with my stuff.


00:58:51.886 --> 00:58:53.623
You're still worried
about all your gadgets?


00:58:53.657 --> 00:58:56.796
I'm never gonna find
David without the capsule.


00:58:56.829 --> 00:58:57.731
You're so selfish.


00:58:58.900 --> 00:59:01.138
Well at least I'm
not still running


00:59:01.171 --> 00:59:03.309
around after a human who
blasted me out of his


00:59:03.342 --> 00:59:05.079
life 50 years ago!


00:59:05.847 --> 00:59:08.753
David didn't blast
me, he said he'd...


00:59:09.922 --> 00:59:11.291
Typical.


00:59:11.325 --> 00:59:14.397
A dog and a cat
fighting each other.


00:59:20.443 --> 00:59:21.879
We threw the rest
of your toys out


00:59:21.913 --> 00:59:24.551
but I like this one.


00:59:24.585 --> 00:59:27.357
Almost as handy as this.


00:59:27.390 --> 00:59:30.429
Hey, leave that
alone, it's mine!


00:59:30.463 --> 00:59:35.473
No, it's mine.


00:59:38.412 --> 00:59:39.247
Todd?


00:59:39.280 --> 00:59:41.451
So where's Peck?


00:59:41.485 --> 00:59:43.455
What are you doing here?


00:59:43.489 --> 00:59:44.725
What am I doing?


00:59:44.759 --> 00:59:48.667
What were you
doing back in 1969,


00:59:49.935 --> 00:59:53.843
pushing aside the world's
greatest feline scientist


00:59:54.845 --> 00:59:59.655
so you could blast off
into space in my place?


01:00:01.926 --> 01:00:05.701
After I escaped, I swiftly
learned Hyperlithium


01:00:05.734 --> 01:00:08.539
has different effects
on different animals.


01:00:09.709 --> 01:00:11.511
The effects on dogs
we've already seen


01:00:11.545 --> 01:00:14.952
but on cats the effect was
merely to prolong my life


01:00:14.985 --> 01:00:15.821
while I waited,


01:00:17.691 --> 01:00:22.701
waited 50 years for the rest
of it to fall back to earth.


01:00:23.970 --> 01:00:25.974
I could barely wait
any longer to get rid


01:00:26.007 --> 01:00:30.984
of you two jokers so I could
complete my plan in privacy.


01:00:32.955 --> 01:00:35.559
So wait that was Victor
driving Peck's truck?


01:00:35.593 --> 01:00:37.363
You two set us up!


01:00:37.396 --> 01:00:39.869
Then where the heck is Peck?


01:00:41.037 --> 01:00:42.875
By the look of things
he's out of hospital


01:00:42.908 --> 01:00:44.745
and going to check
out what's happening


01:00:44.779 --> 01:00:48.018
at the old museum
right about now.


01:00:49.387 --> 01:00:51.993
Hey, what's going on in here?


01:00:52.026 --> 01:00:54.932
What the, animals?


01:01:05.386 --> 01:01:07.056
But you said Peck was
gonna use the Hyperlithium


01:01:07.089 --> 01:01:08.893
to do bad stuff to us!


01:01:08.927 --> 01:01:12.935
Oh I'm sure he would
if I don't stop him.


01:01:12.968 --> 01:01:14.571
Humans, pah!


01:01:14.604 --> 01:01:16.742
They just want to lock us up!


01:01:17.911 --> 01:01:20.917
Well, now we're
in charge, Peck!


01:01:35.947 --> 01:01:37.951
Heel boy, heel before Todd!


01:01:54.885 --> 01:01:59.161
It seems I was right about
Hyperlithium's effects on humans.


01:01:59.194 --> 01:02:04.204
Now, once this Hyperlithium
bomb is fully charged


01:02:05.572 --> 01:02:08.947
it'll detonate and then
all the humans in town


01:02:08.980 --> 01:02:13.756
will become servants to
their rightful masters.


01:02:15.159 --> 01:02:17.264
Todd, you won't
get away with this.


01:02:17.297 --> 01:02:20.870
Oh, do I have to
spell out the irony?


01:02:20.904 --> 01:02:24.077
You've been beaten
by a dog and a cat


01:02:24.110 --> 01:02:26.215
who can actually work together.


01:02:33.628 --> 01:02:34.898
- What the?
- Get this off of me!


01:02:37.971 --> 01:02:38.840
Sinclair?


01:02:44.718 --> 01:02:47.791
This way Master
Felix, Master Buddy.


01:02:47.824 --> 01:02:48.960
We don't have much time.


01:02:50.596 --> 01:02:54.271
Get them, get them!


01:02:59.982 --> 01:03:00.884
Sinclair!


01:03:03.723 --> 01:03:04.557
Sinclair?


01:03:07.029 --> 01:03:09.067
I'm terribly sorry sir,


01:03:09.100 --> 01:03:10.870
it seems I won't be
able to serve any


01:03:10.904 --> 01:03:12.073
con-con-con...


01:03:15.413 --> 01:03:16.248
Sinclair


01:03:17.884 --> 01:03:21.792
It's been a privilege
being your c-c-companion.


01:03:34.251 --> 01:03:38.426
No 80's throwback robot is
going to stand in our way.


01:03:38.459 --> 01:03:40.696
David will stop you!


01:03:40.730 --> 01:03:41.664
Oh really?


01:03:41.698 --> 01:03:43.168
David?


01:03:43.201 --> 01:03:48.078
Well let me tell you, David
invented the Hyperlithium!


01:03:48.813 --> 01:03:50.182
He was a scientist!


01:03:50.216 --> 01:03:52.721
He knew it was dangerous,
that's why he sent


01:03:52.754 --> 01:03:55.793
a dumb animal to fly
it instead of a human.


01:03:55.827 --> 01:03:56.996
No!


01:03:57.029 --> 01:04:00.169
You think you were
being some sort of hero?


01:04:00.202 --> 01:04:02.440
David used you, Buddy!


01:04:02.474 --> 01:04:06.482
He didn't love you and
he's never coming back!


01:04:06.515 --> 01:04:08.151
No, no, no, no, no, no!


01:04:08.185 --> 01:04:10.122
David was my friend!


01:04:47.229 --> 01:04:49.801
Okay, when I get there
I'm going to call you and...


01:04:51.939 --> 01:04:52.774
Whoa.


01:04:56.247 --> 01:04:59.421
Gather 'round,
people, gather round.


01:05:04.531 --> 01:05:08.238
Okay, so we
attack with lasers.


01:05:09.206 --> 01:05:10.376
And fire piranhas
into their eyeballs.


01:05:10.410 --> 01:05:13.849
Codename: operation
Hopeless Cause.


01:05:16.922 --> 01:05:17.557
Daddy?


01:05:19.528 --> 01:05:21.832
Daddy, what have the
animals done to you?


01:05:26.342 --> 01:05:28.412
Oh Daddy, you were right.


01:05:49.253 --> 01:05:50.890
I already have a sticker.


01:05:53.496 --> 01:05:56.100
Heh, yeah, I got
you pretty good.


01:05:58.271 --> 01:05:59.441
I need your help, Buddy.


01:06:01.478 --> 01:06:03.181
There's a kid out
there who thinks


01:06:03.214 --> 01:06:05.286
animals are mean and nasty.


01:06:05.319 --> 01:06:08.292
I need to show her we
can be more than that.


01:06:09.428 --> 01:06:10.363
Humans
are the mean ones.


01:06:11.432 --> 01:06:12.500
That's what you said.


01:06:12.534 --> 01:06:13.369
Maybe.


01:06:14.538 --> 01:06:16.542
You used to believe
people were good.


01:06:16.575 --> 01:06:19.648
And I believe in you.


01:06:19.681 --> 01:06:21.452
I'm just a dog.


01:06:21.485 --> 01:06:23.656
And I'm just a cat
with a silly mask


01:06:23.689 --> 01:06:25.593
who wanted everyone
to think he was cool.


01:06:25.626 --> 01:06:28.332
You're the real hero, Buddy!


01:06:28.365 --> 01:06:30.101
You've been into space.


01:06:30.135 --> 01:06:32.373
You can run faster
than, well, you know.


01:06:32.407 --> 01:06:34.377
And you're strong.


01:06:34.411 --> 01:06:36.448
You're the strongest
person I know.


01:06:37.750 --> 01:06:39.454
And that's why I got you this.


01:06:49.374 --> 01:06:51.678
Triple ply carbon fiber.


01:06:53.449 --> 01:06:55.353
You're not just a dog, Buddy.


01:06:56.220 --> 01:06:57.490
You are Stardog!


01:07:16.728 --> 01:07:18.432
- What the?
- What?


01:07:28.887 --> 01:07:30.188
How's that happened?


01:07:31.458 --> 01:07:33.395
Hey, what's that sound?


01:07:39.441 --> 01:07:40.409
What the what?


01:07:48.224 --> 01:07:48.860
Whoa!


01:08:09.434 --> 01:08:10.937
Thank you, thank you.


01:08:10.971 --> 01:08:13.542
Stand back, Superpets
coming though.


01:08:17.985 --> 01:08:19.286
Give it up Todd.


01:08:19.319 --> 01:08:20.790
Leave the humans alone.


01:08:20.823 --> 01:08:23.495
Yeah, let's show them
how great pets can be,


01:08:23.529 --> 01:08:25.466
how they can trust us
and we can show them


01:08:25.499 --> 01:08:26.735
how to be better people.


01:08:26.768 --> 01:08:30.275
That was long-winded,
Buddy can you summarize?


01:08:30.308 --> 01:08:31.511
Woof!


01:08:31.545 --> 01:08:33.549
Couldn't have said
it better myself.


01:08:33.582 --> 01:08:36.421
Now let me just
get one thing clear.


01:08:36.455 --> 01:08:39.561
Did you two really think
that I would work on this


01:08:39.594 --> 01:08:44.037
for 50 years and not
have some backup plan


01:08:44.070 --> 01:08:46.441
in case a couple of Superpets


01:08:46.475 --> 01:08:48.579
turned up to rain on my parade?


01:08:49.748 --> 01:08:51.384
It does sound
kind of sensible.


01:08:52.520 --> 01:08:54.724
You stole my thunder
once before Buddy,


01:08:54.758 --> 01:08:57.329
you won't stop me this time.


01:08:57.362 --> 01:09:01.471
And you, Felix, everyone
thinks you're a bit of jerk!


01:09:02.640 --> 01:09:04.043
Did you know about this?


01:09:04.077 --> 01:09:07.416
My control of
Hyperlithium's power


01:09:07.450 --> 01:09:10.389
is far greater than yours.


01:09:10.422 --> 01:09:11.725
As you shall now observe.


01:09:24.417 --> 01:09:25.052
Huh?


01:09:39.581 --> 01:09:44.591
Darn kid!


01:09:58.953 --> 01:10:00.556
OK Super-Victor's
a problem, sure,


01:10:00.589 --> 01:10:02.928
but even if we beat
him the real problem


01:10:02.961 --> 01:10:04.430
is Todd and the
Hyperlithium Bomb.


01:10:04.464 --> 01:10:05.866
We need a way to neutralize him.


01:10:05.900 --> 01:10:07.905
Affirmative, he's a cat!


01:10:07.938 --> 01:10:09.407
What's his weakness?


01:10:10.876 --> 01:10:11.711
Catnip.


01:10:16.521 --> 01:10:17.690
Of course!


01:10:17.723 --> 01:10:19.560
We can get some
in the Mega Store.


01:10:19.594 --> 01:10:20.596
Come on Felix.


01:10:21.564 --> 01:10:22.199
Catnip.


01:10:27.009 --> 01:10:29.180
Er, I think it might
be best if I go alone.


01:10:29.213 --> 01:10:30.917
I'll be back soon as I can.


01:10:37.596 --> 01:10:41.137
OK, now all we need to do
is get the dog under control.


01:10:41.171 --> 01:10:42.707
But how.


01:10:42.740 --> 01:10:44.243
Ah, well we've got all these...


01:10:44.277 --> 01:10:46.514
There must be a way to
get him rounded up, think!


01:10:46.548 --> 01:10:48.819
Suggest we use
maximum prejudice.


01:10:48.852 --> 01:10:51.024
I said, we've got all the...


01:10:51.057 --> 01:10:53.228
Quiet, I'm trying to think!


01:10:53.261 --> 01:10:54.797
Ugh!


01:10:54.831 --> 01:10:57.770
Will you all just shut
up and listen to me!


01:11:03.248 --> 01:11:08.091
I said we've still got
all the broken gadgets


01:11:08.125 --> 01:11:10.829
and robot parts they
threw out of the museum.


01:11:10.863 --> 01:11:15.839
Plus, we've got access to a
tactical operations goldfish.


01:11:18.645 --> 01:11:19.680
Oh yeah!


01:11:27.696 --> 01:11:28.732
The park is closed.


01:11:30.936 --> 01:11:33.875
I'm sorry, were
you talking to me?


01:11:33.909 --> 01:11:36.781
Or, or to him?


01:11:43.829 --> 01:11:46.701
Commence operation Fish Tank!


01:11:48.939 --> 01:11:51.144
Fish tank?


01:11:51.177 --> 01:11:53.115
Is that a joke?


01:11:53.148 --> 01:11:54.083
Negative.


01:12:44.450 --> 01:12:48.358
I'm a tactical
operations goldfish!


01:13:00.882 --> 01:13:03.321
I am not going
back inside there.


01:13:04.591 --> 01:13:06.761
It's time for humans
to get locked up.


01:13:09.568 --> 01:13:14.777
They might be human, but I
believe deep in my heart that


01:13:15.580 --> 01:13:18.385
humans are good and
we should be looking


01:13:18.418 --> 01:13:19.820
out for them right now!


01:13:20.989 --> 01:13:24.864
Please, will you use
your powers to help me


01:13:26.067 --> 01:13:29.206
so I can be united with an owner
as their loyal, loving pet.


01:13:31.110 --> 01:13:35.252
That is the lamest
thing I have ever heard.


01:13:36.354 --> 01:13:37.189
Really?


01:13:38.091 --> 01:13:39.927
How about if I do this?


01:13:43.234 --> 01:13:44.036
Cut that out.


01:13:47.943 --> 01:13:49.180
Let's play catch!


01:14:01.638 --> 01:14:04.143
Now what was that
about playing catch?


01:14:04.176 --> 01:14:06.114
Oh, someone wants
to play catch?


01:14:22.146 --> 01:14:23.682
Not again!


01:14:25.419 --> 01:14:27.423
I can't breathe in here!


01:14:29.093 --> 01:14:31.732
I can't
believe that worked!


01:14:31.765 --> 01:14:36.274
It only works on some
stupid dog, is what it does!


01:14:36.307 --> 01:14:40.081
Yeah, well that's what happens
when animals work together!


01:14:41.217 --> 01:14:46.026
Well, I won't make
the same mistake twice.


01:14:53.141 --> 01:14:56.180
Hey, I thought Guardian was
supposed to protect animals?


01:14:56.214 --> 01:14:57.784
Hah!


01:14:57.817 --> 01:15:02.125
It's been hard being
a stray for 50 years.


01:15:02.159 --> 01:15:05.532
Now, with this Hyperlithium
Powered machine


01:15:05.566 --> 01:15:10.576
I'll finally be able to treat
humans like they treated me!


01:15:12.614 --> 01:15:14.684
Er, what do we do now Felix?


01:15:14.718 --> 01:15:15.853
Huh?


01:15:15.887 --> 01:15:18.525
Now would be a good time
to show Todd your shopping.


01:15:20.295 --> 01:15:21.832
Whoa, whoa, whoa, slow down.


01:15:21.865 --> 01:15:23.702
When you get that out


01:15:23.736 --> 01:15:26.073
I can't be held
accountable for my actions.


01:15:27.677 --> 01:15:29.581
What are you two
doing down there?


01:15:29.614 --> 01:15:30.750
OK, ready?


01:15:39.199 --> 01:15:39.834
Cat nip!


01:15:47.215 --> 01:15:48.852
Er, come and get it.


01:15:50.555 --> 01:15:51.390
Give it to me!


01:15:51.424 --> 01:15:53.127
Give it to me now!


01:15:53.862 --> 01:15:55.565
Sorry, what was that?


01:15:55.600 --> 01:15:57.837
I can't hear you
over the faint hum


01:15:57.870 --> 01:16:00.575
of my micro filtered
air conditioning.


01:16:09.560 --> 01:16:10.930
What happened?


01:16:10.963 --> 01:16:11.765
Did we win already?


01:16:11.798 --> 01:16:13.301
Is it nap time?


01:16:13.334 --> 01:16:15.806
Uh, something about
air conditioning?


01:16:16.942 --> 01:16:18.746
Oh, right.


01:16:19.648 --> 01:16:21.250
Where was I?


01:16:21.283 --> 01:16:26.293
Oh yes, how hard it is
being a stray for 50 years.


01:16:27.730 --> 01:16:30.736
Well how about I show you
what that was like, huh?


01:16:39.821 --> 01:16:43.361
How do you like that
Hyperlithium power, huh?


01:17:15.960 --> 01:17:18.564
You disgusting creatures!


01:17:24.878 --> 01:17:27.015
O, where are they?


01:17:27.048 --> 01:17:30.823
I sure hope I don't step
on them by accident!


01:17:33.594 --> 01:17:34.998
Come back!


01:17:35.031 --> 01:17:37.637
I'm not finished with you yet!


01:17:40.142 --> 01:17:42.880
Ugh, they're horrible
stinky strays!


01:17:42.914 --> 01:17:44.082
Clean them up!


01:18:08.966 --> 01:18:13.976
Let's put these dirty strays
out with the rest of the trash!


01:18:14.777 --> 01:18:15.713
Hey, Todd


01:18:17.582 --> 01:18:18.752
Abracadabra.


01:18:23.795 --> 01:18:24.964
No, sunbeam!


01:18:28.104 --> 01:18:28.939
So sleepy.


01:18:32.980 --> 01:18:34.817
Way to go Cassidy!


01:18:34.851 --> 01:18:36.053
Felix, she made a...


01:18:38.491 --> 01:18:40.729
He always was a
sucker for that.


01:18:40.763 --> 01:18:42.098
So sleepy.


01:18:42.132 --> 01:18:45.806
I was headed out of
town when I saw you on TV.


01:18:45.839 --> 01:18:49.079
All the theatrics with
the crowd and the capes,


01:18:49.112 --> 01:18:50.950
it was almost...


01:18:50.983 --> 01:18:52.018
Magical?


01:18:53.188 --> 01:18:56.995
No, it was the stupidest
thing I've ever seen in my life.


01:18:57.028 --> 01:19:01.204
But you're working
together, it's impressive.


01:19:03.675 --> 01:19:07.649
Oh, will you shut up?


01:19:09.220 --> 01:19:11.725
Tinted glass, pretty neat, huh?


01:19:13.127 --> 01:19:14.129
Oh, right.


01:19:15.164 --> 01:19:16.000
Cassidy.


01:19:17.135 --> 01:19:18.271
You know I'm actually
glad you're here


01:19:18.305 --> 01:19:22.679
so I can tell you how pointless
and nauseating G.U.A.R.D.


01:19:22.713 --> 01:19:25.219
was and how much
fun I had hiding


01:19:25.252 --> 01:19:30.061
how your Guardian was secretly
being fully weaponized.


01:19:34.069 --> 01:19:34.904
Todd, you don't
have to do this.


01:19:36.140 --> 01:19:38.211
Yes I do, I want you dead.


01:19:39.847 --> 01:19:41.284
Now, how do I aim this thing?


01:19:44.689 --> 01:19:46.160
There we go!


01:19:46.194 --> 01:19:49.633
Now I just line up the
target with the little


01:19:49.666 --> 01:19:52.105
dot of light...


01:20:31.217 --> 01:20:33.321
It's alright, it's gone now.


01:20:35.259 --> 01:20:37.162
I'm gonna get that
spot of light one day.


01:20:38.899 --> 01:20:39.867
Hey, is that?


01:20:40.936 --> 01:20:42.239
Grandpa, Grandpa!


01:20:42.273 --> 01:20:43.341
Where are you?


01:20:43.375 --> 01:20:44.209
I'm coming!


01:20:45.812 --> 01:20:47.283
I thought Victor scared
all the humans away!


01:20:48.752 --> 01:20:50.087
And my Hyperlithium Bomb


01:20:50.121 --> 01:20:52.359
is still ticking
down to detonation.


01:20:52.393 --> 01:20:57.101
When it goes off her
and her stupid grandpa


01:20:57.135 --> 01:20:58.772
will become my slaves.


01:21:00.242 --> 01:21:02.513
Felix, we've got
to do something...


01:21:15.973 --> 01:21:17.175
Felix!


01:21:17.208 --> 01:21:18.278
Sorry kids.


01:21:18.311 --> 01:21:20.315
It's the only way to stop
the bomb enslaving Alex.


01:21:20.349 --> 01:21:24.155
But when the bomb goes off
it'll destroy the robot and...


01:21:24.189 --> 01:21:26.126
Yeah, looks like it's my turn


01:21:26.159 --> 01:21:28.197
to take a one way trip
to space now, huh?


01:21:29.433 --> 01:21:30.569
But it's the only
way I can prove


01:21:30.602 --> 01:21:33.140
to Alex that pets are good.


01:21:33.173 --> 01:21:37.248
Felix, you don't have to
do this to impress me, ugh!


01:21:38.985 --> 01:21:40.355
Um, Felix?


01:21:40.389 --> 01:21:41.457
Hey Buddy.


01:21:41.491 --> 01:21:44.062
We made a pretty good team, huh?


01:21:44.095 --> 01:21:46.166
Shame I never got to meet David.


01:21:46.199 --> 01:21:47.101
Ah, Felix...


01:21:48.338 --> 01:21:49.473
No, listen Buddy,
I've been thinking.


01:21:49.507 --> 01:21:52.279
David sent you into space
because he knew the Hyperlithium


01:21:52.313 --> 01:21:54.182
was dangerous and he trusted you


01:21:54.215 --> 01:21:57.155
more than anyone
else to protect it.


01:21:57.188 --> 01:21:59.493
David trusted me?


01:21:59.527 --> 01:22:02.266
David knew you
were a hero, Buddy,


01:22:02.299 --> 01:22:04.403
and you've GOT to believe
he's still out there


01:22:04.437 --> 01:22:05.572
looking for you.


01:22:05.605 --> 01:22:07.309
Do you hear me Buddy?


01:22:07.343 --> 01:22:10.549
You've got to believe,
David loves you.


01:22:10.582 --> 01:22:14.957
Yes, he's a good
person and he loves me!


01:22:14.990 --> 01:22:16.361
Er, Buddy?


01:22:18.163 --> 01:22:19.433
Oh wow, I can fly.


01:22:22.306 --> 01:22:24.510
Oh wow, I can fly!


01:22:24.543 --> 01:22:27.483
StarDog, fetch!


01:23:07.463 --> 01:23:10.335
Don't suppose you've got
any more of that catnip?


01:23:11.771 --> 01:23:14.477
Don't you ever do that again.


01:23:21.223 --> 01:23:22.793
What's happening??


01:23:22.827 --> 01:23:24.430
- Daddy!
- Alex!


01:23:27.134 --> 01:23:28.303
Daddy, did you see that?


01:23:28.338 --> 01:23:30.509
The cat blasted into the sky
in a rocket and then the dog


01:23:30.542 --> 01:23:32.746
here flew up and he saved him!


01:23:32.779 --> 01:23:34.215
It was amazing!


01:23:44.202 --> 01:23:47.609
You're right, oh
my gosh you're right!


01:23:49.346 --> 01:23:53.588
They're not mean, or
nasty or dangerous,


01:23:53.621 --> 01:23:55.425
they saved all of us!


01:23:56.828 --> 01:24:00.234
These animals are heroes!


01:24:12.726 --> 01:24:14.663
Daddy, can we keep them?


01:24:14.697 --> 01:24:18.438
You bet honey,
Grandpa will love it.


01:24:18.471 --> 01:24:19.473
Where is Grandpa?


01:24:19.506 --> 01:24:20.342
Grandpa!


01:24:21.945 --> 01:24:23.715
You darned kids!


01:24:23.748 --> 01:24:26.354
Never listened to a word I said!


01:24:27.556 --> 01:24:32.399
I told you I was waiting,
waiting for the day I hear a dog


01:24:33.601 --> 01:24:37.576
can fly and I know that
my Buddy has come back.


01:24:38.544 --> 01:24:39.380
Buddy?


